> tar: I don't know what this is or how to convert it.

tar stands for tar, the Tape Archiver (another UNIX utility).

.tar.Z is a very common format so there should be uncompressing
utilities for it for the Mac. You need an UNIX (un)compress compatible
program (or gzip (that's GNU Zip, _not_ normal zip)) and a tar
dearchiver...

